+- **Recorded from round 2's reviews, not fixed in TASK-059 (non-blocking; leads).** (1) `resolve` quotes a spaced runner path for `cmd.exe /c` so that cmd strips the outer quotes when the line holds more than two: `npm test -- "a b"` with npm under `C:\Program Files\nodejs` exits 1 with `'C:\Program' is not recognized` (fails closed; a `C:\Program.exe` would run, which needs write access to C:\). (2) A UNC value (`\\host\share`) of a folder option or of an environment name is touched by `os.path.isdir` and `realpath` before the roots check refuses it, so Windows opens an SMB connection with the user's credentials first: refuse UNC and `\\?\UNC\` forms by their text before any filesystem call. (3) `os.path.relpath` raises `ValueError` where a value and the launch folder differ in drive form (`\\?\E:\...`, a subst drive): the launcher fails closed with a traceback instead of exit 125. (4) The builder's `_package_link` lets `_winapi`'s ImportError through off Windows where a symbolic link fails.
